Design for Refill at Home is a design strategy that focuses on creating packaging that can be refilled and reused by consumers in their own homes. This approach aims to reduce single-use packaging waste and encourage a more sustainable consumption behavior. By designing packaging that is durable and easy to refill, companies can promote a circular economy by extending the lifespan of their products and reducing the need for new packaging materials. Examples of companies implementing this strategy include Loop, a global shopping platform that offers refillable packaging for a wide range of products, and Ecover, a cleaning products company that provides refill stations in stores for customers to refill their bottles.